│     │       │   └─0 text "Correctness"
│     │       ├─1 text ": These rules flag code that is outright wrong as written. If you encounter a\ncorrectness issue, you should try to fix it rather than suppressing the error with "
│     │       ├─2 inlineCode "noqa"
│     │       ├─3 text " or\n"
