│     │       ├─1 text ": These rules are similar to "
│     │       ├─2 inlineCode "correctness"
│     │       ├─3 text " lints in that the code is likely wrong,\nbut "
│     │       ├─4 inlineCode "suspicious"
│     │       └─5 text " lints acknowledge that there are valid reasons for the code to be written in this\nway. You will still typically want to fix these issues, but using a suppression comment may\noccasionally be necessary. Deprecations generally also fit into this category."
